The function is already a thin lookup, so I only tightened the branch into a single conditional return, removing the separate named-pointer/early-return structure to give the compiler a marginally simpler control-flow to inline.

```cpp
    FIT_BOOL IsAvgCombinedPedalSmoothnessValid() const
    {
        const Field* field = GetField(63);
        return (FIT_NULL == field) ? FIT_FALSE : field->IsValueValid();
    }
```